target:    src/Schema/Meta.php
gate:      php tests/lease-claim-shape-test.php
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    the steal condition is not `expired (dt < %d) or already mine`
rationale: Inverts the lease steal condition — dt > now steals every UNEXPIRED lease, so any concurrent claimer takes a live lease and the single-flight the lease exists to provide is gone. SchemaMetaTest cannot see this: its double never executes SQL, so only the shape gate reads the condition. This is the exact mutation class PITFALLS 21/22 warns about — same green with and without the defect — unless the gate pins the literal condition.
---
diff --git a/src/Schema/Meta.php b/src/Schema/Meta.php
index 4fdc1fe7..ff297aae 100644
--- a/src/Schema/Meta.php
+++ b/src/Schema/Meta.php
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ final class Meta
         $written = $db->query($db->prepare(
             "INSERT INTO {$prefix}slim_meta (meta_key, meta_value, dt) VALUES (%s, %s, %d)
              ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE
-                 dt         = IF(meta_value = VALUES(meta_value) OR dt < %d, VALUES(dt), dt),
+                 dt         = IF(meta_value = VALUES(meta_value) OR dt > %d, VALUES(dt), dt),
                  meta_value = IF(dt = VALUES(dt), VALUES(meta_value), meta_value)",
             $key,
             $holder,
